      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9c9d2a47-7c04-5f8a-b2a5-36cbfbd29d80",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Vaidotas, Wojdat, Kęstutis, Algirdas, Jogaila\n- Roles: son of Kęstutis, Grand Duke of Lithuania, ruler of medieval Lithuania, Duke of Trakai\n- Places: Lithuania, Kreva\n\nFacts:\n- Kęstutis was born around 1297.\n- Kęstutis was a ruler of medieval Lithuania and the Duke of Trakai.\n- From 1342 to 1377, Kęstutis governed the Grand Duchy of Lithuania together with his brother Algirdas.\n- In 1362, Vaidotas, also called Wojdat, was recorded as a son of Kęstutis, Grand Duke of Lithuania.\n- From 1377 to 1381, Kęstutis governed the Grand Duchy of Lithuania together with his nephew Jogaila.\n- Kęstutis died on 3 August or 15 August 1382 in Kreva.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
